G1303.def:
δια-τίθημι 
[in LXX chiefly for כָּרַת, frequently δ. διαθήκην (כָּרַת) ;] 
to place separately, arrange, dispose. Mid, only in NT; 
__1. (a) in general, to dispose of; with dative of person(s), to assign to one, Luc 22:29; 
__(b) to dispose of by a will, make a testament (in cl., δ. διαθήκην also in this sense): Hébreux 9:16-17 (but cf. R, mg., and see: διαθήκη). 
__2. δ. διαθήκην, to make a covenant (Aristoph.): with dative of person(s), Hébreux 8:10 (LXX); before πρ, with accusative of person(s), Actes 3:25, Hébreux 10:16" (LXX) (cf. ἀντι-διατίθημι).†

G1318.def:
διδακτός, -ή, -όν
(διδάσκω), [in LXX: Ésaïe 54:13 (לִמּוּד), 1Ma.4:7 * ;] 
__1. that can be taught. 
__2. taught; with genitive, of source of teaching (in cl., poët. only); 
__(a) of persons: δ. θεοῦ, Jean 6:45 (LXX); 
__(b) of things, λόγοις δ. πνεύματος, 1 Corinthiens 2:13.†

G1329.def:
δι-ερμηνεύω 
[in LXX: 2Ma.1:36 * ;] 
intensive of ἐρμηνεύω, to interpret; 
__(a) to explain, expound: with accusative, Luc 24:27; absol., 1 Corinthiens 12:30 14:5 14:13 14:27; 
__(b) to translate: Actes 9:36.†

G1330.def:
δι-έρχομαι 
[in LXX for אֵבֶר, הָלַךְ, בּוֹא, etc. ;] 
__1. to go through, pass through; 
__(a) of things: Matthieu 19:24, Marc 10:25, Luc 2:35, al.; 
__(b) of persons: Luc 19:4; with accusative loc., Luc 19:1, Hébreux 4:14, Actes 12:10; before διά, with genitive loc., Matthieu 12:43, 1 Corinthiens 10:1; before εἰς, Marc 4:35; ἕως, Luc 2:15. 
__2. to go about: Luc 9:6, Actes 20:25; of a report, to spread, go abroad (Thuc.), Luc 5:15

G1340.def:
δι-ισχυρίζομαι (T, Rec. διϊσ-), depon.; 
__1. to lean upon. 
__2. to affirm confidently: with ptcp., Luc 22:59; with accusative and inf. (Bl., § 70, 3), Actes 12:15.†

G1344.def:
δικαιόω, -ῶ
(δίκαιος), [in LXX chiefly for צָדַק pi., hi., (1) as Eze.16:51, Jérémie 3:11 (cf. NT usage); (2) as Deutéronome 25:1; Exode 23:7, Ésaïe 50:8 ;] 
__1. in cl., 
__(a) with accusative of thing(s), to deem right; 
__(b) with accusative of person(s), to do one justice; pass., δικαιοῦσθαι, to be treated rightly, opposite to ἀδικεῖσθαι. 
__2. In NT, as in LXX, and as usual with verbs in -όω from adjectives of moral meaning; 
__(1) to show to be righteous: Matthieu 11:19, Luc 7:35, Romains 3:4" (LXX), 1 Timothée 3:16; 
__(2) to declare, pronounce righteous: Luc 7:29 10:29 16:15 18:14, Romains 2:13 3:24, 26 3:28 4:5 8:30, 33, Tite 3:7; before ἀπό, Matthieu 11:19, Luc 7:35, Actes 13:39, Romains 6:7; ἐκ πίστεως, Romains 3:30 5:1, Galates 2:16 3:8, 24; ἐξ ἔργων, Romains 3:20 (LXX) Romains 4:2, Galates 2:16, Jacques 2:21, 24-25; ἐκ τ. λόγων, Matthieu 12:37; διὰ τ. πίστεως, Romains 3:30; with dative, Romains 3:24, 28, Tite 3:7; before ἐν, Actes 13:39, Romains 3:4 5:9, 1 Corinthiens 4:4 6:11, Galates 2:17 3:11 5:4, 1 Timothée 3:16 (see Cremer, 193, 693; DB, ii, 826 ff.).†

G1377.def:
διώκω 
[in LXX chiefly for רָדַף ;] 
__1. to put to flight, drive away: Matthieu 23:34. 
__2. to pursue; 
__(a) of persons; with accusative, without hostility, to follow after: Luc 17:23; with hostile purpose: Actes 26:11, Apocalypse 12:13. Hence, to persecute: Matthieu 5:10-12, 44 10:23, Luc 11:49 21:12, Jean 5:16 15:20, Actes 7:52 9:4-5 22:4, 7-8 26:14-15 Romains 12:14, 1 Corinthiens 4:12 15:9, 2 Corinthiens 4:9, Galates 1:13, 23 4:29 5:11 6:12, Philippiens 3:6, 2 Timothée 3:12; 
__(b) metaphorically, with accusative of thing(s), of seeking eagerly after: Romains 9:30, 1 Timothée 6:11, 2 Timothée 2:22; νόμον δικαιοσύνης, Romains 9:31; τ. φιλοξενίαν, Romains 12:13; εἰρήνην, Hébreux 12:14, 1 Pierre 3:11; τὰ τῆς εἰ., Romains 14:19; τ. ἀγάπην, 1 Corinthiens 14:1; τὸ ἀγαθόν, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:15; absol., to follow on, drive, or speed on (Æsch.), Philippiens 3:12, 14.†
